  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3754",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is likely to interact with Kcnf1 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine binds to Kcna6 or Kcnv2, both of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, which in turn is associated with Kcnf1. This indicates that Dalfampridine may influence Kcnf1 through a common mechanism involving the delayed rectifier potassium channel pathway. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific molecular interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple binding sites and participation in similar functional roles implies that Dalfampridine may modulate Kcnf1 through a broader cellular mechanism, possibly by affecting the activity of delayed rectifier potassium channels.",
